<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">The Wretched of the Earth</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1961">1961</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Les Damnés de la Terre</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Wretched of the Earth is a book by the Martinique-born psychiatrist and writer <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frantz-fanon">Frantz Fanon</a>, published in French in 1961 shortly before his death, with a preface by Jean-Paul Sartre. Drawing on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algerian-war">Algerian War</a> of Independence, in which Fanon supported the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-liberation-front-south-yemen">National Liberation Front</a>, it analyses the psychology of colonialism and defends violent struggle against it. It became a central text of anti-colonial and Black liberation movements.</p></div>
